{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUBUw1G76bWzMamuNrdxLN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-538\"\n3\ttitle = \"Arm the complexity sensor here at the ruled scope, and re-base the module-size ratchet to SLOC (OI-68 phase 2, 1c)\"\n4\tspecref = \"\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = [\"WI-537\", \"~WI-521\"]\n8\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Deliverable\n14\t\n15\tExecuted OI-68 phase 2 at the ruled shape **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a** — arm + re-base,\n16\tnever arm + retire. Both sensors stay armed on different axes; nothing was deleted\n17\tand no pointer moved.\n18\t\n19\t1. **Armed (3a).** New `[step:complexity]` in `docs/stack.ini`\n20\t   (`command = {py} project-trajectory/scripts/check_complexity.py --root . --mode\n21\t   enforce`, `layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) — the exact-equality\n22\t   compare against `docs/complexity-baseline` in both directions, nonzero on\n23\t   either. Minted no spine row: `SR-183` already carries both postures (\"gated only\n24\t   where a repo opts in\"), and the opt-in is the step's presence here.\n25\t   `check_complexity.py`'s module docstring updated from \"report-only as shipped\" to\n26\t   \"report-only where shipped, armed here\". Shipped default stays report-only\n27\t   (that's phase 3, a separate WI).\n28\t\n29\t2. **Scoped (2a).** `check_complexity.DEFAULT_INCLUDE` widened to census `tests/`\n30\t   as well as `project-trajectory/scripts/`; `docs/complexity-baseline` re-stamped\n31\t   to seed the 20 `tests/` functions over threshold 15 (census now 200 rows: 180\n32\t   scripts + 20 tests). This closes WI-521 §3's sensor gap on the complexity axis;\n33\t   WI-521 amended in place to record that, and to state honestly what is still\n34\t   unwatched (test-tree *size* growth — no function crossing cognitive 15 — is\n35\t   watched by neither armed sensor).\n36\t\n37