{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cea8Wo3b9nSewsj1NGHVX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FJNW5u1Azfk5YpQtWeLzmL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Peter\\.claude\\projects\\C--Projects-ai-template\\memory\\worker-agents-background-full-suite.md","old_string":"**What actually happens:** the run keeps going in background; the agent ends its turn \"waiting\"; a completion notification later re-invokes it and it finishes the close (worked for WI-503). One resume nudge may still be needed if the agent mis-times its wait.\n\n**How to apply:** either accept the auto-background + notification cycle (budget one extra round-trip per full-suite worker and don't scold the worker for it), or direct the BATCHED form docs/status.md already names for this box: split the suite into <10-min chunks run foreground (e.g. two halves by test directory, same basetemp hygiene, quote both totals). Never treat a \"waiting for the suite\" stop as a fabrication risk — the worker is doing the honest thing. Related: [[ai-template-complexity-audit]].","new_string":"**What actually happens — and the trap (refined 2026-08-30, WI-538 close):** in an orchestrator/persistent session the background run survives and a completion notification re-invokes the agent. BUT in a `scripts/agent_loop.py --wi` WORKER session, ending the turn while the suite runs in the background gets the background task KILLED on session teardown (`\"status\":\"killed\"`) — the suite never finishes and no close happens. WI-538 sat open across TWO reaped resume sessions (iteration logs 003/004) for exactly this: each launched `-n auto` in the background, ended its turn, and was reaped with the run killed. A third session finally closed it by NOT backgrounding.\n\n**How to apply:** in a `--wi` worker, prefer the BATCHED FOREGROUND form — partition the ~145 test files into <10-min chunks and run each foreground with the max 600s timeout, quoting each total. Clean split that guarantees full single-pass coverage: import `tests/conftest.py::SLOW_MODULES` (via `importlib` — a root `conftest.py` shadows it), run the fast in-process modules as one batch (~40s, ≈ the smoke set) and the ~71 slow subprocess/scaffold modules in two halves (~3.5 min + ~9 min on a loaded box). Union across disjoint batches = every file once. On this box WI-538 got 3191 passed / 16 skipped / 0 failed that way. A single-shot `-n auto` full run times out at 600s when the box is loaded by other sessions. NB the file list a Python `open('w')` writes gets CRLF — strip with `tr -d '\\r'` before feeding paths to pytest, or collection returns exit 5 (\"no tests ran\"). Never treat a \"waiting for the suite\" stop as a fabrication risk — but in a worker, don't rely on the notification cycle; finish the run in-turn. Related: [[ai-template-complexity-audit]], [[unattended-run-2026-08-30-traps]]."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1692,"cache_read_input_tokens":145065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1692},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a5f524-44ec-4973-a9db-b50119b38249","uuid":"c70fb6b7-d2b4-492b-950f-e40eb4c0aa3d","request_id":"req_011Cea8WnBVnDCHVYMkqf6Y1"}
