{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cea8Xodb7wBKPWk9qzeWQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-538 is closed. Summary:\n\n## WI-538 — done and closed\n\nThis was a **resumed worker session**. The build (arm + re-base) was already committed on the branch by earlier sessions; what remained was **verifying the full suite and closing the row** — and the row had stayed open because the two prior resume sessions (iteration logs 003/004) each launched the full suite in the *background*, ended their turn, and were **reaped with the background run killed** before it could finish.\n\n**What I did this session:**\n\n1. **Reviewed the build for correctness** — confirmed `module_sloc` is cleanly factored and shared by both sensors (pure refactor of `sloc`; scoring logic unchanged), the 9 re-based `BASELINE` values match the documented raw→SLOC map, `[step:complexity]` mirrors its live sibling sensors, and no spine/registry rows were touched.\n\n2. **Verified everything green:**\n   - Arming: `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` → `OK - 200 row(s) over 15, unchanged from baseline`, exit 0\n   - Commit bar: smoke 1427 passed / 6 skipped (43.9s); smoke budget 38.1s vs 60s\n   - **Full unfiltered suite: 3191 passed, 16 skipped, 0 failed** — run in three disjoint file-partition batches in the *foreground* (the box is loaded past the 10-min single-shot timeout), each file run exactly once across all 145 test files\n   - Live `check_trajectory`: clean, exit 0 (546 WIs; WI-538 now among the done)\n\n3. **Closed the row** (C6 ritual): Deliverable filled before Context, `specref` cleared, spec moved via `spec_move.py` to `docs/archive/work/complete/`, empty claim dir removed, log fragment's Verification section filled with the real pastes. No spine rows minted → no approval-brief regen. Two commits: telemetry logs alone, then the close carrying `WI: WI-538` (I caught and corrected an initial slip where `spec_move`'s staged rename got swept into the telemetry commit — re-split so the close commit properly carries the trailer).\n\n**Working tree is clean; branch ready for the integrator's queue.**\n\nI also refined the `worker-agents-background-full-suite` memory to record the reap-on-teardown trap: in a `--wi` worker, don't rely on backgrounding the suite — finish it in-turn via the batched foreground form."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":146757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1158},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a5f524-44ec-4973-a9db-b50119b38249","uuid":"b22f108b-2c9a-4f13-ba66-bcc3c6d74192","request_id":"req_011Cea8XngY4V67Jr5i23Jw3"}
